    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Gunnar Henderson** (71.11), who represent our strongest offensive upside against favorable matchups. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a high-ceiling 4.55 xERA pairing against Trey Yesavage, with his dynamic platoon advantage providing the necessary spark to push him into the elite tier. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a cornerstone despite a slight dip from his base projection due to the platoon dynamic against Noah Cameron; his role at the top of the order and the elevated park factor in his venue help maintain his efficiency score well above the 70 mark. **Kyle Tucker** (69.61) also serves as a critical anchor, maintaining an elite efficiency score despite the lack of a prominent lineup boost, largely driven by his consistent base projection against Brandon Pfaadt.\n\nStrategic adjustments for today include prioritizing **Coby Mayo** (66.04) and **Andy Pages** (66.83), both of whom see significant score inflation from favorable park factors. **Andy Pages** is particularly intriguing; the combination of a positive matchup against Pfaadt and a slow delivery from the opposing battery creates an ideal environment for him to exploit the stolen base scarcity in our 5x5 scoring. On the bench, **Miguel Vargas** (51.82) was the most difficult exclusion. While his 0.398 xwOBA is elite, the optimizer opted for **Liam Hicks** and **Jacob Wilson** because their high-order placement provided a more reliable path to run production, whereas **Miguel Vargas** was squeezed out by the sheer depth of our starting outfield and corner infield options.\n\nInvestors should monitor the weather and lineup statuses carefully, as several key bats\u2014including **Drake Baldwin**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Josh Jung**\u2014remain pending official confirmation. **Jorge Polanco** was considered for a utility spot but ultimately benched due to a 45% rain risk and a difficult matchup agains